          "id": "SP_EUPLEXAURA_ARBUSCULA_BROCH_1935",
          "name": "Euplexaura arbuscula Broch, 1935",
          "rank": "SPECIES",
          "commonName": "",
          "lineage": "Euplexaura",
          "subspeciesCount": 0,
          "description": "Branches thread-like. Calyces dome-shaped, arranged all around the branches (Figure 2 b). Polyps without sclerites. The surface layer of the coenenchyme has spindles and blunt ellipsoids (Figure 5 a), up to 0.15 mm long, with complex tubercles. The interior has small spindles, capstans, and a few crosses, up to 0.15 mm long (Figures 5 b-d), all with simple tubercles.",
